{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"27b51326bb431bc728462e81e7a5c565d96b77c3fa88756e02974ee2b9848633","packTokens":2620,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":208,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1128,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1178,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using authorized Folio3 Google accounts and have employee and vehicle profiles populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking and schedule releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can receive notifications and claim available spaces first-come, first-served.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record verification attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and automatically email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What should each role be able to view and do, especially security guards handling verification and administrators handling employee-level reports?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Employees see their own records; guards see the information needed to verify entry; administrators manage records and see configured reports.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"If a temporary claimant has multiple registered vehicles, which plate or plates should the entrance check accept for that employee's claim?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Accept any vehicle plate registered to the claimant for the claimed date.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"When claim requests arrive at nearly the same time for the last available space, how should the system determine which request is first?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The first request accepted by the service gets the space; later requests fail and see refreshed availability.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What evidence should count as an actual vehicle entry for utilization reporting, rather than merely a camera detection or authorization attempt?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have security record whether the vehicle actually entered after the check.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should existing employee, dedicated-space, floor, and registered-vehicle records be loaded for launch?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Parking administrators enter the initial records in the app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Can a temporary parking user cancel a successfully allocated claim, and what happens to that space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"An employee may cancel at any time, and the space becomes available immediately.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should security guards and parking administrators authenticate, given that Google sign-in is specified for employees but not for these roles?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require Folio3 Google accounts for guards and administrators as well.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Who selects and maintains the stakeholders who receive the weekly utilization email?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Parking administrators manage the report recipient list in the app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 21 requirements for one implementation run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 21 requirements be approved for one implementation run, or should the work be split or reduced?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"The release action confirms “Released”; the current parking status is “Claimable” once its availability time arrives (immediately for post-time same-day releases), then “Claimed” after allocation.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the release confirmation and the parking’s current status be represented when a release is not yet claimable, or becomes claimable immediately?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Drop the pre-authorization restriction; administrators can directly add, update, and remove report recipients.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Should administrators be able to add report recipients directly, or should the pre-authorization restriction remain, and if so, how should the initial authorized list be established?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"How should actual entry by a permanent-sticker vehicle be recorded for utilization, given that it bypasses temporary authorization verification?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record LPR-detected entry for utilization without performing authorization verification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Should an employee be able to cancel a successful temporary claim, and if so, who may cancel it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Remove temporary-claim cancellation; a successful claim remains assigned.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict sign-in to authorized Folio3 Google Workspace accounts, assign application roles, and deny access when the corporate-directory employee profile cannot be identified or retrieved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Identify employees by corporate email, use the corporate directory for employee IDs and names, and maintain parking status, floor assignments, and registered vehicles in the app, preserving the plate captured on existing claims when profile plates change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Require non-dedicated employees to save at least one vehicle plate before accessing the dashboard, while keeping vehicle make, model, and color optional and directing incomplete returning profiles to registration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Enforce role-based access: employees can access only their own records, guards receive only information needed for entry verification, and administrators can manage records and access configured reports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Let administrators maintain parking-space inventory, floors, dedicated holders, parking assignments, and vehicles, including initial launch records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Let dedicated holders release or schedule releases for their parking, prevent duplicate releases for the same holder and date, limit scheduling to 30 calendar days ahead, and make releases claimable according to a configurable office-local release time that defaults to 08:00.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Show release confirmation as “Released” and report parking as “Reserved” before availability, “Claimable” when available, and “Claimed” after allocation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Publish the current available-space count and notify eligible employees without dedicated parking when spaces become claimable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee request accepted by the service, limit employees to one temporary claim per date, and keep successful claims assigned for that date without employee cancellation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Record each successful claim’s date, time, employee, and assigned space, and show the assigned floor without requiring proof of arrival on that floor.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Process LPR detections for cars, ignore non-car objects, and bypass temporary verification for vehicles with permanent parking stickers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"For readable plates on unstickered vehicles, verify against a temporary claim for the current office-local date using any plate registered to the claimant for the claimed date, and activate the green indicator only for valid authorization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When plates cannot be read or verified, or a camera, authorization service, or indicator is unavailable, make no automated authorization or green-indicator activation and record the failure or outage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Record every temporary verification attempt and let security record whether the vehicle actually entered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Record permanent-sticker LPR entries as utilized parking without authorization verification, and use guard-recorded actual entry—not camera detections or authorization attempts alone—to determine temporary utilization and identify unused dedicated parking and temporary claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Generate and email a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office-local timezone to configured stakeholders, covering the preceding complete Monday-to-Sunday week and including unused-parking employees, daily and weekly statistics, released-space and temporary-claim totals, and an overall utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Let administrators add, update, and remove weekly-report email stakeholders in the app without requiring recipient pre-authorization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Provision the first parking administrator from a deployment-configured Folio3 account and let administrators assign employee, security-guard, and administrator roles to other authorized Folio3 accounts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}